{% block extra %}
## `ab_test_data` and `get_ab_test`

`ab_test_data` and `get_ab_test` are the same method under two names. The
library's docs and tutorial use `get_ab_test`, the name of the analysis tools
(`get_ab_bootstrap`, `get_sample_ratio`, `get_conversion_rate`);
`ab_test_data` exists so that every widget has a `<widget>_data` twin. The
full parameter and column reference is on the
[A/B Test Scorecard](/docs/tools/get-ab-test) page.

See also the two A/B tools that have no widget:
[`get_sample_ratio`](/docs/tools/get-sample-ratio), the sample ratio check to run
before reading any metric, and [`get_ab_bootstrap`](/docs/tools/get-ab-bootstrap),
the joint bootstrap replicates behind contrasts between periods.

